summary:
  The backfill asks for a logo without saying which address the station is saved at.

history:
  The station's own directory record is the one row that proves whose logo
  this is, and it is found by the saved address. Without it the picker has
  the name alone, and for "Rock FM" or "Radio Nova" the name alone lends
  nothing, so every such station would keep its initials for ever while the
  library's own tests stayed green.

target:
  package/contents/ui/main.qml

find:
                  fav = FaviconLogic.pickFavicon(rows, norm, HealLogic.normName, st.host, 30);

replace:
                  fav = FaviconLogic.pickFavicon(rows, norm, HealLogic.normName, "", 0);

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_invariants.py::test_a_logo_found_by_name_passes_the_donor_gate_at_both_doors.
  Line-neutral.
